# Who reviews what.
#
# This file is the repository-file half of code review automation. It is read by
# GitHub when it routes a review request. It is *not* a substitute for branch
# protection: required status checks, required reviews, and whether `main` refuses
# a direct push are repository settings, set in the repository's settings, and are
# listed in `docs/ci-cd.md` under "settings that live outside the repository".
#
# The reason this file is a single owner rather than a team is that the repository
# is a single maintainer's work. A CODEOWNERS file that invents a team the
# maintainer has not created would be a file that looks like governance and does
# nothing.

# Default owner for everything not matched more specifically below.
* @PBMINE

# The architectural core. Every change here can change guest-visible behaviour,
# so it is called out separately even though the default already covers it: a
# reviewer skimming `crates/` should be able to see which directories the ISA, the
# interpreter and the memory model live in.
crates/lazalith-isa/      @PBMINE
crates/lazalith-cpu/      @PBMINE
crates/lazalith-memory/   @PBMINE
crates/lazalith-machine/  @PBMINE
crates/lazalith-devices/  @PBMINE
crates/lazalith-types/    @PBMINE

# The specification. `instruction.md` is the Phase-I roadmap and `binstruction.md`
# is the Beyond-Lazalith specification; a change to either is a change to what
# the project is, and should not be made as a side effect of a code change.
instruction.md             @PBMINE
binstruction.md            @PBMINE

# The reproducible build and the CI that depends on it.
flake.nix                  @PBMINE
flake.lock                 @PBMINE
.github/                   @PBMINE
